damage around here, too.

261
00:16:06,320 --> 00:16:08,680
Look, do you see that little girl? Yeah.

262
00:16:08,980 --> 00:16:11,077
Her mother promised to
buy her something with her

263
00:16:11,160 --> 00:16:14,337
money that used to be in the
bank before this happened.

264
00:16:14,420 --> 00:16:15,250
You know her?

265
00:16:15,333 --> 00:16:16,673
Nah, I just made it up.

266
00:16:17,640 --> 00:16:20,757
What are you doing worrying
about other people's money?

267
00:16:20,840 --> 00:16:22,958
I mean, what good's it gonna do you?

268
00:16:23,360 --> 00:16:24,242
Nothing at all.

269
00:16:25,420 --> 00:16:26,250
Except...

270
00:16:26,333 --> 00:16:28,420
That the situation is not equal.

271
00:16:45,060 --> 00:16:46,280
What's he doing?

272
00:16:54,280 --> 00:16:57,817
What do you think you're doing
trying to play the hero cowboy?

273
00:16:57,900 --> 00:16:59,097
No, not really.

274
00:16:59,180 --> 00:17:00,457
I'm not as great as you might think.

275
00:17:00,540 --> 00:17:01,370
I am.

276
00:17:01,453 --> 00:17:07,297
Ah gee,

277
00:17:07,380 --> 00:17:08,210
that's too bad.

278
00:17:08,293 --> 00:17:09,357
You've got a flat tire.

279
00:17:09,440 --> 00:17:11,734
Well, I guess you won't be escaping in.

280
00:17:26,860 --> 00:17:30,877
How'd he do that?

281
00:17:30,960 --> 00:17:32,037
Are you crazy?

282
00:17:32,120 --> 00:17:35,617
Do you have any idea what you're
getting yourself into, mister?

283
00:17:35,700 --> 00:17:40,080
This gentleman here is the one and
only infamous humanoid typhoon!

284
00:17:40,280 --> 00:17:42,040
He's Vash the Stampede!

285
00:17:42,400 --> 00:17:43,460
Now that's funny.

286
00:17:44,180 --> 00:17:45,010
Pardon me.

287
00:17:45,240 --> 00:17:48,617
But I was under the impression
that he was a lot more handsome.

288
00:17:48,700 --> 00:17:51,582
Are you implying that I
am not Vash the Stampede?

289
00:17:52,040 --> 00:17:53,700
Maybe we should find out.

290
00:17:55,880 --> 00:17:56,710
Huh?

291
00:18:06,220 --> 00:18:07,050
Why?

292
00:18:10,160 --> 00:18:11,860
Why are you doing this?

293
00:18:12,060 --> 00:18:14,660
We can use force if we have to. Right.

294
00:18:16,860 --> 00:18:17,690
Why?

295
00:18:19,020 --> 00:18:21,440
Hold it right there! Huh? Huh?

296
00:18:33,520 --> 00:18:36,600
This gun is an original
Frank Marlin special,

297
00:18:36,940 --> 00:18:39,697
and don't think I'll miss
just cause I'm a woman.

298
00:18:39,780 --> 00:18:42,604
Am I supposed to be afraid
of this Frank Marlin?

299
00:18:42,700 --> 00:18:44,406
It's a Russian piece of crap!

300
00:18:44,500 --> 00:18:47,500
You actually believe you'll
hit me with that thing?

301
00:18:49,700 --> 00:18:50,530
Why?

302
00:18:50,613 --> 00:18:52,420
Why are they doing that?

303
00:18:54,680 --> 00:18:56,780
Why am I just standing here?

304
00:18:57,500 --> 00:18:59,620
That this situation is not equal.

305
00:19:02,900 --> 00:19:03,730
Huh?

306
00:19:06,940 --> 00:19:08,060
What the?

307
00:19:23,500 --> 00:19:25,497
Apparently you think that you have won.

308
00:19:25,580 --> 00:19:26,600
You think wrong!

309
00:19:32,540 --> 00:19:34,177
A piece of parting advice.

310
00:19:34,260 --> 00:19:36,731
You should always save your aces for last.

311
00:19:42,600 --> 00:19:43,659
Checkmate, mister.

312
00:19:45,860 --> 00:19:48,331
Shooting from behind is just not my style.

313
00:19:49,300 --> 00:19:50,476
You'll pay for this!

314
00:19:50,700 --> 00:19:52,020
You will pay!

315
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:55,882
Wow, they really stick together.

316
00:19:56,620 --> 00:19:57,450
Huh?

317
00:19:59,420 --> 00:20:00,560
Wasn't even loaded.

318
00:20:02,400 --> 00:20:03,420
Sure wasn't.

319
00:20:06,880 --> 00:20:08,937
He's actually dumber than I thought.

320
00:20:09,020 --> 00:20:10,491
That guy is unbelievable.

321
00:20:13,640 --> 00:20:16,405
Here's to all the great
folks to save the town!

322
00:20:16,580 --> 00:20:17,920
In your way!

323
00:20:23,860 --> 00:20:26,640
Grandma, what'd you wait for? Fill her up!

324
00:20:27,500 --> 00:20:30,497
I mean, please fill her up,
miss, if you wouldn't mind.

325
00:20:30,580 --> 00:20:31,420
That's better.

326
00:20:33,200 --> 00:20:35,000
I will never understand him.

327
00:20:35,360 --> 00:20:37,177
Things turned out well after all.

328
00:20:37,260 --> 00:20:39,025
There's no damage to the town.

329
00:20:39,140 --> 00:20:41,277
The chief will probably
give us both promotions.

330
00:20:41,360 --> 00:20:43,300
But the bandit was a fake.

331
00:20:43,460 --> 00:20:44,695
It wasn't really him.

332
00:20:44,860 --> 00:20:48,657
And we still haven't gotten our
chance to meet Vash the Stampede.

333
00:20:48,740 --> 00:20:50,858
But someone matches his description.

334
00:20:52,440 --> 00:20:55,360
Oh, man, I've got to find
the can. Stick him up.

335
00:21:05,140 --> 00:21:08,905
I wouldn't exactly count on this
for everyday use if I were you.

336
00:21:09,080 --> 00:21:10,040
Here, take it.

337
00:21:11,380 --> 00:21:13,737
I've changed the cylinder
to the hammer parts for you.

338
00:21:13,820 --> 00:21:15,291
I gave it a full tune-up.

339
00:21:16,100 --> 00:21:16,980
Hey, thanks.

340
00:21:17,520 --> 00:21:19,696
Oh, heck, you don't need to thank me.

341
00:21:20,080 --> 00:21:22,197
But there is one thing I want to know.

342
00:21:22,280 --> 00:21:24,574
What are you going to do with that gun?

343
00:21:25,880 --> 00:21:29,477
I intend to use it to create equality
and peace throughout the world!

344
00:21:29,560 --> 00:21:31,160
Huh? Huh? Huh?

345
00:21:36,120 --> 00:21:40,577
Well if you ever wear it out again
bring it back I'll fix it as good as new

346
00:21:40,660 --> 00:21:45,937
great when I do I'll Bring the bourbon
next time no thanks I've given up alcohol

347
00:21:46,020 --> 00:21:50,837
I've got better things to do instead
of Drinking what do you think they're

348
00:21:50,920 --> 00:21:55,740
talking about shh you know what I just
realized pal I never did forget your name.

349
00:21:56,020 --> 00:21:58,120
Well, uh, I'm, uh...

350
00:22:04,600 --> 00:22:06,060
You drink too much.

351
00:22:06,480 --> 00:22:07,480
I'm sorry!

352
00:22:08,080 --> 00:22:08,910
Disgusting!

353
00:22:14,040 --> 00:22:17,857
You just don't want to admit that
you're worried about him, do you, Mary?

354
00:22:17,940 --> 00:22:20,857
No, and I'm not following
him for your information.

355
00:22:20,940 --> 00:22:23,646
We just happen to be
going the same direction.

356
00:22:26,940 --> 00:22:28,760
Bang! Bang!

357
00:23:09,000 --> 00:23:10,317
Thank

358
00:23:10,400 --> 00:23:11,717
you

359
00:23:11,800 --> 00:23:18,800
so

360
00:23:22,060 --> 00:23:24,980
much for watching.

361
00:23:25,120 --> 00:23:29,317
He has nothing to do with what we need.

362
00:23:29,400 --> 00:23:34,060
I'm a smile that will be perfect.

363
00:23:35,600 --> 00:23:41,577
It will be perfect for the future.

364
00:23:41,660 --> 00:23:45,817
I'll see you

365
00:23:45,900 --> 00:23:50,240
next time.

366
00:23:51,140 --> 00:23:52,160
Na,

367
00:23:52,480 --> 00:23:55,020
na, na, na, na,

368
00:23:58,340 --> 00:24:04,920
na, na, na.

369
00:24:05,940 --> 00:24:09,760
A past that can't be
forgotten and can't be buried.

370
00:24:10,360 --> 00:24:14,080
A past that can't even be
shaken for just a little time.

371
00:24:14,620 --> 00:24:18,457
The sentiment deep inside each of
their hearts is strong and equal.

372
00:24:18,540 --> 00:24:22,260
For beloved parents and
for a beloved daughter,

373
00:24:22,800 --> 00:24:26,329
two men can only find the answer
from behind their triggers.

374
00:24:26,460 --> 00:24:31,225
The moment the sentimental bullets flew
towards each other, the men stood silent.

375
00:24:32,220 --> 00:24:34,580
Yet were weeping, the past enslaved.
